h the total time now the determining factor, the event favored slalom specialists. The event one day was delayed because of poor weather. The leader after the downhill was " [:a {:href "/athletes/82343"} "Katja Seizinger"] " with " [:a {:href "/athletes/83038"} "Pernilla Wiberg"] " close behind in second. This made Wiberg the favorite because she was a better slalom skier. But on the first run, Wiberg caught a tip on a gate near the finish and did not finish. Seizinger was steady in the slalom, placing fifth in that section, to win her third Olympic gold medal. She was followed by her two teammates, " [:a {:href "/athletes/81037"} "Martina Ertl"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/81135"} "Hilde Gerg"] " (winner of the slalom gold in Nagano), giving Germany only the fourth medal sweep in Olympic Alpine skiing, after Austria in 1956 men’s giant slalom, Austria in 1964 women’s downhill, and Norway in 1994 men’s combined."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {} "Downhill"] [:th {} "Slalom"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/82343"} "Katja Seizinger"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} "2:40.74"] [:td {} "1:28.52 (1)"] [:td {} "1:12.22 (5)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "14"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/81037"} "Martina Ertl"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} "2:40.92"] [:td {} "1:29.76 (4)"] [:td {} "1:11.16 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [: